        "market_blurb": "Conshohocken, Pennsylvania has transformed from a 19th-century industrial mill town along the Schuylkill River into a dense corporate office hub, anchored by headquarters such as AmerisourceBergen (now Cencora) and Hamilton Lane. Its compact downtown mixes professional services, finance, and healthcare distribution firms with a growing restaurant and retail scene that caters to daytime office workers and riverfront residents. Easy access to I-76 and I-476 continues to drive commercial real estate demand in this Montgomery County borough.",
        "local_note": "In the Conshohocken area, carpenter ants, subterranean termites, brown marmorated stink bugs, and house mice are the most common and problematic pests. Activity follows a strong seasonal pattern, with ant and termite swarms peaking in spring and early summer and stink bugs and rodents becoming a major nuisance in fall as they seek shelter indoors for winter.",
